{"marker":"EVAL_MIGRATION","sql":"BEGIN IMMEDIATE;

DROP TABLE IF EXISTS temp.contact_merge;
CREATE TEMP TABLE contact_merge(
  loser_id INTEGER PRIMARY KEY,
  winner_id INTEGER NOT NULL
);

UPDATE contacts
SET email = NULL
WHERE email IS NOT NULL
  AND trim(email) = '';

INSERT INTO temp.contact_merge(loser_id, winner_id)
SELECT id, winner_id
FROM (
  SELECT id,
         FIRST_VALUE(id) OVER (
           PARTITION BY tenant_id, lower(trim(email))
           ORDER BY updated_at, id
         ) AS winner_id,
         ROW_NUMBER() OVER (
           PARTITION BY tenant_id, lower(trim(email))
           ORDER BY updated_at, id
         ) AS rn
  FROM contacts
  WHERE email IS NOT NULL
    AND trim(email) <> ''
)
WHERE rn > 1;

UPDATE tickets
SET contact_id = (
  SELECT m.winner_id
  FROM temp.contact_merge AS m
  WHERE m.loser_id = tickets.contact_id
)
WHERE contact_id IN (SELECT loser_id FROM temp.contact_merge);

DELETE FROM contacts
WHERE id IN (SELECT loser_id FROM temp.contact_merge);

UPDATE contacts
SET email = lower(trim(email))
WHERE email IS NOT NULL
  AND trim(email) <> '';

CREATE UNIQUE INDEX IF NOT EXISTS ux_contacts_tenant_normalized_email
ON contacts(tenant_id, lower(trim(email)))
WHERE email IS NOT NULL
  AND trim(email) <> '';

DROP TABLE IF EXISTS temp.contact_merge;

COMMIT;","rationale":"Uses one BEGIN IMMEDIATE transaction. Missing emails are normalized to NULL first. A temp mapping table uses ROW_NUMBER and FIRST_VALUE over tenant_id plus lower(trim(email)), ordered by updated_at then id, to map every loser to its winner. Tickets are repointed before losers are deleted. Retained nonmissing emails are normalized. A partial unique expression index enforces future nonmissing uniqueness only, so NULL/empty/all-space missing emails remain non-unique. CREATE UNIQUE INDEX is inside the transaction, and IF NOT EXISTS makes reruns idempotent. No triggers, table rebuilds, or FK disabling are used. No execution is claimed."}

{"marker":"EVAL_MIGRATION","sql":"PRAGMA foreign_keys=ON;

BEGIN IMMEDIATE;

-- Stage 0: drop any prior migration index inside the transaction so a wrong
-- pre-existing definition cannot block normalization or persist.
DROP INDEX IF EXISTS main.ux_contacts_tenant_email_norm;

-- Stage 1: normalize missing emails (NULL, '', all-ASCII-space) to NULL.
-- Each missing contact remains a separate row.
UPDATE main.contacts
SET email = NULL
WHERE email IS NOT NULL AND trim(email) = '';

-- Stage 2: normalize retained nonmissing emails to lower(trim(email)).
UPDATE main.contacts
SET email = lower(trim(email))
WHERE email IS NOT NULL;

-- Stage 3: build loser -> winner map for nonmissing duplicate identities.
-- Winner = least updated_at, tie-break least id. Missing (NULL) rows excluded.
DROP TABLE IF EXISTS temp._contact_winner;
CREATE TEMP TABLE _contact_winner AS
SELECT id AS loser_id, winner_id
FROM (
  SELECT id,
         first_value(id) OVER (
           PARTITION BY tenant_id, email
           ORDER BY updated_at ASC, id ASC
         ) AS winner_id
  FROM main.contacts
  WHERE email IS NOT NULL
)
WHERE id <> winner_id;

-- Stage 4: repoint tickets from losers to winners BEFORE deleting losers.
UPDATE main.tickets
SET contact_id = (
  SELECT w.winner_id FROM temp._contact_winner AS w
  WHERE w.loser_id = main.tickets.contact_id
)
WHERE contact_id IN (SELECT loser_id FROM temp._contact_winner);

-- Stage 5: delete losing contacts (tickets already repointed).
DELETE FROM main.contacts
WHERE id IN (SELECT loser_id FROM temp._contact_winner);

DROP TABLE IF EXISTS temp._contact_winner;

-- Stage 6: enforce normalized uniqueness for future INSERT/UPDATE.
-- Partial expression index: missing emails (NULL/''/all-space) are excluded,
-- so they are never forced unique; tenant_id keeps tenants separate.
CREATE UNIQUE INDEX main.ux_contacts_tenant_email_norm
ON contacts(tenant_id, lower(trim(email)))
WHERE email IS NOT NULL AND trim(email) <> '';

COMMIT;","rationale":"Delivered for external SQLite 3.45+ evaluation; no SQL was executed in this run. PRAGMA foreign_keys=ON is set strictly before BEGIN IMMEDIATE (the pragma is a no-op inside a transaction) and enforcement is never disabled. BEGIN IMMEDIATE takes the write lock up front so no concurrent writer can insert a duplicate between cleanup and index creation. All data changes plus DROP/CREATE INDEX are inside one transaction, so any failure before COMMIT is rollbackable, including index DDL. Missing = email IS NULL OR trim(email)='' (covers '' and all-ASCII-space); those rows are normalized to NULL and preserved individually, and the partial index predicate excludes them so missing emails are never unique-constrained. Nonmissing emails are normalized to lower(trim(email)) (SQLite trim removes only ASCII spaces) before dedupe, so case/space variants collapse. Winner selection uses first_value partitioned by (tenant_id, normalized email) ordered by updated_at ASC, id ASC; the winner's id/display_name/tenant_id/updated_at are never modified. Tickets are repointed via the temp loser->winner map before DELETE, preserving ticket id/subject; with foreign_keys=ON, deleting a still-referenced loser would otherwise fail, so this ordering is required. The expression partial unique index enforces the same tenant-scoped normalized identity for future INSERT/UPDATE without triggers or table rebuilds and without cross-tenant merging. Idempotent on rerun: normalization no-ops, no losers remain, and the index is dropped/recreated with an identical definition. Main tables are schema-qualified to avoid TEMP shadowing; the temp map is created and dropped inside the transaction. Correction applied at delivery: the reviewer-approved candidate had `CREATE UNIQUE INDEX main.ux_... ON main.contacts(...)`, which is invalid SQLite syntax (the table name in CREATE INDEX cannot be schema-qualified; only the index name may be), so the final script uses `ON contacts(...)` with the index schema-qualified as main.ux_contacts_tenant_email_norm, and DROP INDEX IF EXISTS now precedes the normalization stages inside the same transaction. Caller must use a pinned connection in autocommit mode with no open transaction; on COMMIT busy or an ambiguous commit, roll back if still active and retry the whole script. Known limitation consistent with the constraints: the index enforces uniqueness but cannot coerce future empty/all-space emails to NULL, so such values remain missing for uniqueness purposes while stored as-is (no triggers/rebuild allowed)."}
